# Local agent tooling. Everything under .claude/ is per-machine assistant setup
# -- hooks, settings, and generated config -- and none of it is shared.
#
# Deny-by-default with NO exceptions, on purpose. An earlier `!.claude/hooks/`
# carve-out was justified as "self-contained and useful to any contributor":
# true of those scripts' contents, false of their filenames and provenance
# markers, which shipped in the repo as a result. An exception for one path
# also leaves the next path the tooling invents equally exposed.
.claude/

# direnv: `.envrc` is committed and holds no values; the real ones live here.
.envrc.local
.direnv/

# Assistant tooling output. Kept on the machine that produced it, not shared.
docs/superpowers/
